### Pre-existing baseline note (not caused by PS-05)

On unmodified `origin/master`, `npm run typecheck` fails with a pre-existing test-only error:

```text
lib/progression/lifecycle.test.ts(52,32): error TS2802: Type 'Set<LifecycleStage>' can only be
iterated through when using the '--downlevelIteration' flag or with a '--target' of 'es2015' or
higher.
BASELINE_TYPECHECK_EXIT=2
```

This baseline failure was reproduced with PS-05's changes stashed at the same base. PS-05 carries
the identical one-line test-only unblock already used by sibling patch sets PS-01/PS-03
(`Array.from(new Set(stages))`) so the typecheck gate can pass. No runtime code is affected.

